      "en": "### Useful EASTIE Spaces\n\nClassroom  \nLego area  \nConstruction / block room  \nSmall outdoor grass area attached to PK classroom  \nIndoor physical fitness area  \nSandpit when appropriate  \nCircle-time area / mat area  \nTable activity area  \nToy shelf and classroom storage  \nTheatre / pretend play space\n\n### Useful Materials\n\nBalls  \nToy cars  \nBlocks  \nLego / Duplo bricks  \nLarge wooden blocks  \nLarge soft blocks  \nTeddies  \nDolls  \nTrains  \nToy roads / tracks  \nBoxes  \nBags  \nBaskets  \nTransparent storage boxes  \nShelves  \nTables  \nChairs  \nRoad mats  \nToy houses  \nGarages  \nScarves / covering fabric  \nMystery bags  \nVisual clean-up cards  \nTurn-taking tokens\n\n### Enhanced Resource Opportunities\n\nThe Lego area and construction room can support roads, garages, houses, shelves, bridges, and toy homes. Boxes and baskets remain essential for in/out and clean-up routines. Tables, chairs, shelves, and mats provide concrete on/under spatial contexts. Outdoor spaces can support larger car-road or ball play if safety boundaries are clear.",
